    "lawSection": "Transportation",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S3809A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act in relation to directing the New York city\ntransit authority and the metropolitan transportation authority to\nreport to the governor and the legislature on transportation service\nreductions and eliminations occurring since January 1, 2010\n\nPURPOSE:  To determine the extent to which service has been eliminated\nor reduced by the New York City Transit Authority and the Metropolitan\nTransit Authority since January 1, 2010.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill requires the New York City Transit Authority\nand the Metropolitan Transit Authority (MTA) to report all service\nreductions and eliminations occurring after January 1, 2010, as well\nas the restoration of any services, to the Governor and the\nLegislature by December 31, 2016. This report is required to include a\nlist of reduced or eliminated service routes, fare increases, restored\nservices, and a geographic breakout of the affected communities.\n\nSection two of the bill provides that provides that this act shall\ntake effect immediately.\n\nEXISTING LAW: New law\n\nJUSTIFICATION:  As fares continue to rise, this report will provide a\nclear picture of the service cuts and eliminations of transportation\nservices in the MTA region since January 1, 2010. While the Governor\nstated in Veto Message 238 of 2013 that this report is not necessary\nbecause the MTA planned to restore some eliminated services and\nestablish new service, the fact that the MTA now seeks to raise fares\nand has not restored all reduced or eliminated service begs the\nquestion of the necessity of this report.\n\nThis report will highlight the extent of the service eliminations and\nreductions implemented by the MTA, as well as their impact on all of\nthe people who live in New York City.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:  2014: S.6469 - Referred to Transportation 2013:\nS.5025 - Veto Message 238 2012: S.7625 - Referred to Transportation\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: None\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:  This act shall take effect immediately\n\n",
